 {"message":"I understand the political math on your side, but that four-point swing is exactly the size of what abstention is worth to you — you're not paying me for agreement, you're paying me to not bring the whole thing down. +2 isn't a favour I'm asking for, it's the threshold below which I can't tell my own voters this was worth staying out of the way for. Below that, I'm better off letting you sweat over FF or MI.

If the number itself is the sticking point for your base, I can work with how it's framed — a binding climate investment commitment, a specific target, something concrete enough that it reads as +2 in substance even if you want to argue about the label. What I won't do is come down to +1 or take vague language and call it a deal. That's a non-starter for me and you'd be back here inside a year anyway when it falls apart in public.

So here's where I am: give me the substance of +2 on environment, in whatever form your drafters want to dress it, and Green Voice stays out of your way. Anything less, and I'd rather take my chances with the voters than own a compromise that erases what my 42 seats are here for.","ending":"continue"}
